    LLM: 'Game: Three Nought Four. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: '304 is a trick-taking partnership game for four. 32-card deck. Card values: J=30, 9=20, A=11, 10=10, K=3, Q=2, 8=7=0. Total 304 points. Bid from 160 in tens; highest bidder sets trump face-down then remaining cards dealt. Follow suit; bidding team must make bid in points. Popular in Sri Lanka and India.',
    objective: 'Each team aims to bid a number (in multiples of 10, from 160 upward) and then win at least that many card points in tricks. The bidding team wins the hand if they make their bid; otherwise the opponents win.',
